{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,24]],"date-time":"2026-10-24T03:32:43Z","timestamp":1792812763354,"version":"4.5.0"},"reference-count":263,"publisher":"World Scientific Pub Co Pte Ltd","issue":"29","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Int. J. Mod. Phys. B"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2005,11,20]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Showing that the location of the zeros of the partition function can be used to study phase transitions, Yang and Lee initiated an ambitious and very fruitful approach. We give an overview of the results obtained using this approach. After an elementary introduction to the Yang\u2013Lee formalism, we summarize results concerning equilibrium phase transitions. We also describe recent attempts and breakthroughs in extending this theory to nonequilibrium phase transitions.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1142\/s0217979205032759","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2005,11,24]],"date-time":"2005-11-24T06:33:58Z","timestamp":1132814038000},"page":"4269-4329","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":159,"title":["STATISTICAL MECHANICS OF EQUILIBRIUM AND NONEQUILIBRIUM PHASE TRANSITIONS: THE YANG\u2013LEE FORMALISM"],"prefix":"10.1142","volume":"19","author":[{"given":"IOANA","family":"BENA","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Theoretical Physics Department, University of Geneva, 24, Quai Ernest Ansermet, CH-1211 Geneva 4, Switzerland"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"MICHEL","family":"DROZ","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Theoretical Physics Department, University of Geneva, 24, Quai Ernest Ansermet, CH-1211 Geneva 4, Switzerland"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"ADAM","family":"LIPOWSKI","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Quantum Physics Division, Faculty of Physics, A. Mickiewicz University, Ul. Umultowska 85, 61-614 Pozna